{"name":"Superstar","hex":"#ffcc11","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"superstar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone who has accumulated a vast amount of fame; a high-level celebrity.","An exceptionally productive employee."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superstar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Superstar","blocks":[{"text":"A superstar is someone who has great popular appeal and is widely known, prominent, or successful in their field. Celebrities referred to as \"superstars\" may include individuals who work as actors, musicians, athletes, and other media-based professions."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superstar","wikidata":"Q1209526"},{"title":"Superstar (Delaney and Bonnie song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Superstar\" is a 1969 song written by Bonnie Bramlett and Leon Russell that has been a hit for many artists in different genres in the years since. The best-known versions are by the Carpenters in 1971, Luther Vandross in 1983, and Sonic Youth in 1994."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superstar_(Delaney_and_Bonnie_song)","wikidata":"Q6122411"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Mary_Woronov_by_David_Shankbone.jpg/500px-Mary_Woronov_by_David_Shankbone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Mary_Woronov_by_David_Shankbone.jpg/1280px-Mary_Woronov_by_David_Shankbone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Mary_Woronov_by_David_Shankbone.jpg/500px-Mary_Woronov_by_David_Shankbone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In the 1960s and 1970s, Andy Warhol popularized the term \"superstar\" to describe people like actress Mary Woronov.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMary_Woronov_by_David_Shankbone.jpg"},{"srcs